      "description": "Watch Union Santa Fe vs Sarmiento Junin highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina delivered a spectacle of high intensity and tactical shifts as Gimnasia LP hosted Sarmiento Junin . On the night of August 29, 2026, both sides displayed incredible resilience in a contest that kept the spectators guessing until the final whistle. Modica Ignites the First Half Sarmiento Junin started the match with aggressive intent, quickly identifying gaps in the Gimnasia LP backline. The star of the show, Agustin Modica , began his clinical display in the 17th minute. Latching onto a well-timed pass from Tomas O'Connor , the striker fired home to break the deadlock. The visitors maintained their momentum, and just before the interval, Agustin Modica struck again in the 39th minute. Capitalizing on a defensive lapse, he secured his second of the game, sending Sarmiento into the locker room with a commanding two-goal cushion. Gimnasia’s Dramatic Fightback Following the break, Gimnasia LP introduced Maximiliano Zalazar and Lucas Janson to spark a revival. The tactical shift paid dividends almost immediately. In the 46th minute, Agustin Auzmendi pulled one back after being set up by Bautista Barros Schelotto . The home side continued to pour forward, and their persistence was rewarded in the 62nd minute. Maximiliano Zalazar clinical finish, courtesy of an assist from Lucas Janson , brought the score level at 2-2, completing a stunning comeback that sent the home crowd into a frenzy. The Final Twist in La Plata With the match hanging in the balance, Agustin Modica stepped up once more to claim the spotlight. In the 76th minute, the forward completed his hat-trick after a decisive ball from Esteban Fernandez , restoring the lead for Sarmiento Junin . The closing stages were a battle of nerves, marked by yellow cards for Fermin Antonini , Nahuel Barboza , and Modica himself. Despite late pressure from the hosts, Sarmiento held firm through eight minutes of stoppage time to secure a memorable 3-2 victory away from home."
