      "description": "Watch Union Santa Fe vs Lanus highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 7, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as the two sides took to the pitch for a high-stakes clash in the Liga Profesional Argentina , held on August 7, 2026. Both teams looked to impose their style of play early on, turning the match into a compelling tactical chess match. A tactical stalemate The first half was characterized by intense physicality and a cautious approach, with neither side willing to give an inch. As the referee kept a tight leash on proceedings—issuing a yellow card to Carlos Izquierdoz at the 41-minute mark—it became clear that the outcome would depend on who could break the deadlock after the interval. Second half fireworks The game burst into life in the second half. Lucas Menossi broke the stalemate in the 53rd minute, putting Union Santa Fe ahead and forcing Lanus to chase the game. The visitors responded with tactical substitutions that shifted the momentum, culminating in a 73rd-minute equalizer from Felipe Pena Biafore , who was set up beautifully by Gonzalo Perez . The drama reached its peak shortly after. In the 77th minute, Joaquin Mosqueira surged forward to finish a clinical move assisted by Cristian Alberto Tarragona , reclaiming the lead for the hosts. Though Lanus pressed until the final whistle—earning a booking for Walter Bou in stoppage time— Union Santa Fe held firm to secure a hard-fought victory in this thrilling match ."
